    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by a high-upside top of the order, headlined by **Corbin Carroll** (82.87) and **Brice Turang** (75.06). **Corbin Carroll** remains the engine of our SB-focused strategy, and his date with Tanner Bibee creates an ideal environment for his speed to thrive against an xERA of 4.46. Similarly, **Brice Turang** sits in a prime position to capitalize on a favorable matchup against a sub-tier arm; his massive +19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill rating makes him our most efficient MI option. **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) also rates as an elite play today, as the combination of a friendly park factor (+14%) and a strong platoon edge against Wacha cements his status as a must-start over lower-ceiling alternatives.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer involved **Travis Bazzana**, who narrowly missed the cut at 47.69. While his matchup against an arm with a 6.32 xERA was enticing, the L/L disadvantage and a lower spot in the order pushed him below the floor established by the remainder of the lineup. We are also keeping a watchful eye on our \"Lineup Pending\" designations, specifically for **Cole Young**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Zach McKinstry**, and **Josh Naylor**. While **Tyler Soderstrom** boasts a strong 62.80 projection thanks to significant park advantages, any late lineup shifts could trigger a re-evaluation of these bench assets to ensure we maintain our daily efficiency targets. We remain cautious with **Austin Riley** (50.12), whose score is tethered by a tough matchup against Griffin and a less-than-ideal spot in the batting order. While **Trevor Story** and **Seiya Suzuki** remain sidelined, the current configuration is optimized to maximize our stolen base potential while maintaining an AVG-friendly floor across the board.",
